  "notes": [
    "**Conducir** is irregular in present and preterite",
    "Present: irregular \"yo\" form (conduzco) with spelling change c→zc before o",
    "Preterite: completely irregular stem \"conduj-\" with special endings (no \"i\" in condujeron)",
    "Imperfect: regular -IR pattern",
    "Future: regular future endings attached to infinitive",
    "Similar conjugation pattern to **traducir** (to translate) and **producir** (to produce)",
    "In Latin America, **manejar** is more commonly used for \"to drive\"",
    "Common usage: *conducir un coche* (to drive a car), *conducir a* (to lead to)"
  ],
